{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1474067-the-irredeemable-the-self-loathing-bankrupt","id":1474067,"title":"The Irredeemable-the self loathing bankrupt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-05T23:02:52-08:00","id":1474067,"title":"The Irredeemable-the self loathing bankrupt","content":"As it turns out, I had ample time for this write up. Inspired by LostLight, I was surprised I really wanted to try a loyalist Slasher, the mechanics are wonky, as that's my weakest point, but I hope the writeup captures themes that feel authentic to the Loyalists of Thule <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;It's too much for you. Let me help you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Responsibility, debt, guilt. These three things unite the Loyalists of Thule. It's what encourages them seek out the secrets of the supernatural. It what motivates them to risk their lives for people they don't know. It's what forces every hunter to feel they have to repay no matter how many times over. The compact believes this to be a deserving fate, for all who have entered the compact have committed sins of such magnitude that there is no other way to repay them except by taking on the loyalist mission. At first it was to repay the sin of setting the foundation for the nazi party. And then passed on to the heirs of those founders. And now, such a debt is repayed by people not even remotely related to it, people who made grevious mistakes that the compact believes to be kin to in spirit. Every single hunter in this compact is reminded of their guilt. Every secret uncovered from a monster is held in contrast to secrets of sins the loyalists themselves keep from the hunters they assist. Every foe killed is a repayment to a debt that will never be repaid in full. The Loyalists of Thule are responsible for these things, and yet, responsibility strengthens a hunters resolve as much as it leaves them sinking in their own guilt.<br /> <br /> Such responsibility defines a loyalist. They feel the need to uncover what they can, to be cautious so mistakes are kept at a minimum, and to make right what went wrong. But the Vigil so often leaves such things in vain. Just like the incident they (or the incident pushed on them) atone for, sometimes things go wrong where they thought all would go right. By the time they uncover the ban and bane of a spirit, a good friend is Claimed. A ritual believed to counteract a witch's only makes things worse. Or maybe it all goes right. It doesn't matter to the loyalist. He feels nothing he does can repay his debt. It certainly doesn't help the compact affirms them there is more to be done. A few come to a terrible realization. A realization that they are Irredeemable.<br /> <br /> The Irredeemable's guilt twists upon itself. The Compact believessuch guilt needs to be repayed, yet these self proclaimed Irredeemable say that's impossible for themselves. Yes, as a collective, it can happen, but for these poor few, it's a pointless exercise. This doesn't lead to apathy, or even sloth. But it doesn't lead to a sense of freedom from responsibility. No, it leads to a hunter that believes he must shoulder the burden of all sins. Whether anyone wants him to or not.<br /> The loyalist, drowning in self hatred, knows he is a lost cause. Others, however, aren't. The others have so much to live for, and the sentimental loyalist cant bear to see them followbthe same path they do. They can have the weight of their guilt taken away, the burden of responsibility transferred, and the debt repaid by the Irredeemable. When over their episodes of regret, these Slashers ferret out the secrets of the sinners, and makes it their mission to alleviate them of their debts. The twisted morality of the hunter deludes himself into thinking that since their debts can't be repaid, they are free to commit terrible acts for the sake of others.<br /> <br /> To the Loyalists of Thule, these Irredeemable are perversions who run counter to the very point of their mission. And yet, they are useful despite their morally bankrupt sense of responsibility. This usefulness lies in the fact they also seek out the guilt of monsters. The Irredeemable have an instinctive empathy with regrets, and they freely share what they learn through interacting with monsters, who are already too as bankrupt as they are. More importantly, these slashers see fellow loyalists as taking responsibility for themselves, and therefore dont bither to atone for their sake. Of course, the average loyalist claims it's crazy to trust a killer. <br /> <br /> Until they feel they are unable to solve a problem themselves. Suddenly, the guilt ridden seems like a reasonable man to ask for help.<br /> <br /> Mechanics<br /> The Irredeemable are a compact specific scourge undertaking. And Loyalist of Thule who develops a ripper undertaking may further develop into this scourge undertaking, and retain the former's talent and frailty as well as the newly attained latter's.<br /> <br /> Attribute: Intelligence or Composure<br /> <br /> Undertaking skills: academics, empathy, occult, investigation, politics, larceny, persuasion<br /> <br /> Talent-debt collector<br /> Tell the slasher your deepest regrets and guilty secrets, and he will absolve you of them by taking responsibility for them himself. Even if you wish not to, he will nonetheless find them out with preternatural skill. When entering a social interaction, the Irredeemable may roll Manipulation+Empathy to ferret out a hidden guilt of the opponent. On a success, the the slasher gains the Informed condition relating to the person he just talked to, but also the guilty condition relating the secret he found out. When acting on this guilt, which inevitably manifests as murder to any actors who helped (directly or indirectly) contribute to the guilty act, the slasher gains the 9 again quality on rolls.<br /> <br /> Frailty-the first debt: after so long taking in the debts of other, the Irredeemablelearns to push back the original reason he ever became a loyalist. When reminded, he suddenly finds himself unable to focus repaying debts. When shown proof of this first debt, the slasher gains the fugue condition. The only way to get rid of it is for the slasher to take a new debt and complete what he considers apt repayment of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}